# Infrastructure-Creator Workflow

This is a PHP accelerator **generator**, not a ready-to-use accelerator. It scans a target PHP project by path, researches its real dependencies/integrations, asks the few questions evidence cannot answer, and generates a bespoke accelerator (`AGENTS.md`, skills, agents, commands, hooks, `memory-bank/`) directly into that target project's own root, for only the AI tool(s) the target team selects.

## Command -> Agent -> Skill

- **Commands** (`.cursor/commands/*.md`) are `/slash` entry points: `infra-scan`, `infra-generate`, `infra-build`, `infra-update`, and `infra-adapt`. Pass the target project path as `$ARGUMENTS`.
- **Agents** (`.cursor/agents/*.md`) each run one skill in an isolated context, then stop - except the five sanctioned orchestrators (`infra-scan`, `infra-generate`, `infra-build`, `infra-update`, and `stack-adapter`).
- **Skills** (`.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`) contain the actual workflow.

Execute only the selected skill, then stop unless it is one of the five orchestrators. Always end with a Context Summary and Next Steps.

## Two-Phase Flow

```text
/infra-scan <target-path>
  -> stack-scanner / architecture-scanner / integration-scanner /
     infra-ops-scanner / security-compliance-scanner / conventions-scanner /
     domain-behavior-scanner (parallel)
  -> stack-researcher -> clarifying-interview -> profile-synthesizer
  -> profile section 8: behavioral contract
  -> profile section 11: generated infrastructure
  -> profile section 12: memory preview

  <-- HUMAN REVIEW CHECKPOINT: read tasks/TASK-{N}/infra-scan-project-profile.md -->

/infra-generate <target-path>
  -> policy-forge / skill-forge / hook-forge / memory-seed (parallel)
  -> agent-forge -> command-forge -> skill-flow-composer
  -> AGENTS.md version stamp + .infra-manifest.json -> bootstrap-verifier
  -> generated domain skills when evidence-gated + operational memory-bank skill

/infra-update <target-path>   (later, after this generator ships a new release)
  -> reads the target's .infra-manifest.json (aborts on legacy targets without one)
  -> replaces only hash-verified untouched files; user-edited files become
     explicit per-file decisions; unlisted files are never touched
  -> rewrites the manifest -> bootstrap-verifier
```

## Workspace Boundary

Infrastructure-Creator stays outside the project it scans/generates for, and every command requires an explicit target-path argument. Never point a command at this folder's own tree. Phase 1 is read-only on the target; Phase 2 is the only writer.
